@startuml dsd_uc2_checkRefundStatus
' NewEra POS - Design sequence diagram, UC2 Handle Returns: checkRefundStatus() (card refund still pending, FR-26 and FR-77), W11
' Team D - editable source of assets/dsd_uc2_checkRefundStatus.png
' Render with: java -jar plantuml.jar -charset UTF-8 -tpng assets/dsd_uc2_checkRefundStatus.puml
' Participants: logical view (architecture.md 4.2). Operations: system_interfaces.md 3.3, 3.7, 4.1 to 4.3; AD-05, AD-07, AD-08, AD-09.
' Messages marked <<new>> are not in the logical view or in system_interfaces.md yet (sent to Borja for the design class diagram).
title DSD UC2 Handle Returns - checkRefundStatus() (card refund still pending, FR-26 and FR-77)
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName Arial
skinparam defaultFontSize 11
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign left
skinparam ParticipantPadding 8
skinparam BoxPadding 6
skinparam NoteBackgroundColor #FFFBE6
skinparam NoteBorderColor #B7791F
skinparam maxMessageSize 190
hide footbox
box "ui.api" #EAF2E3
  participant "ctrl:ReturnController" as C
end box
box "application" #E8EEF7
  participant "h:ReturnHandler" as H
end box
box "domain" #FFF7E0
  participant "r:Return" as R
  participant "f:Refund" as F
end box
box "application.interfaces" #F6EDF7
  participant ":Transaction\nRepository" as TR
  participant ":PaymentService" as PAY
end box

== checkRefundStatus() for one return ==
[-> C : POST /api/returns/{returnID}/refund-status
C -> H : checkRefundStatus()
H -> TR : find(returnID)
TR --> H : r
H -> R : refund()
R --> H : f
alt f is not PENDING
  H --> C : f.state (CARD_REFUNDED or NEEDS_APPROVAL, nothing to ask)
  C -->[ : 200 state
else f is PENDING
  H -> PAY : refundStatus(r.transactionID)
  note right of PAY : the same transaction ID as the refund (IR-02); 10 s timeout in the adapter (AD-07)
  alt APPROVED
    PAY --> H : APPROVED, reference
    H -> F : setState(CARD_REFUNDED, reference) <<new>>
    H -> TR : addRefundStatus(f.id, CARD_REFUNDED, reference)
    note right of TR : new row of refund_status, insert only; also queued for the store database
    H --> C : CARD_REFUNDED
    C -->[ : 200 CARD_REFUNDED
  else DECLINED (the refund failed or is unknown to the Payment Service)
    PAY --> H : DECLINED
    H -> F : setState(NEEDS_APPROVAL) <<new>>
    H -> TR : addRefundStatus(f.id, NEEDS_APPROVAL, null)
    H --> C : NEEDS_APPROVAL
    C -->[ : 200 NEEDS_APPROVAL: the cashier can ask a store manager (approveCashRefund)
  else NOT_AVAILABLE
    PAY --> H : NOT_AVAILABLE
    H --> C : PENDING
    C -->[ : 200 PENDING "Not confirmed yet, ask again later"
  end
end

note over H
  The return was completed when it was confirmed (confirmReturn), so this operation changes only the state of the refund.
  The same steps serve UC5 with RentalReturnHandler (checkRefundStatus on /api/rental-returns/{id}/refund).
  GRASP
  Information Expert: Refund keeps its own state. Controller: the handler asks the Payment Service, the controller does not.
  Indirection, Protected Variations: PaymentService hides the Payment Service; NOT_AVAILABLE is an answer, not an error (AD-07).
  The list of pending refunds of S-02 (listPendingRefunds, FR-77) only reads TransactionRepository.findPendingRefunds; it is not drawn here (open point).
end note
@enduml
